column9:
The hazardous waste carrier shall be committed to the environmental conditions specified in the environmental license and to the following:

Commitment to the content and components of the technical report mentioned in Article (19) of this Decree,

Not to transport any hazardous wastes that are not accompanied by the hazardous waste movement form set by the Ministry of Environment provided that the form accompanies the shipment during all its stages,

Not to transport hazardous wastes that are not packed in the manner stipulated in Article (14), clause (1) of this Decree,

Not to store hazardous wastes at the carrier’s unless he owns an environmentally licensed storage facility from the Ministry of Environment,

Ensure not to deliver the shipment of hazardous wastes to any storage or recovery or treatment or final disposal facility that is not authorized from the Ministry of Environment;

Ensure that the shipment is in conformity with the data documented on the hazardous waste movement form prior to the commencement of the transport;

Assume responsibility for any damage or change to the status of hazardous wastes during transportation and find appropriate ways to manage them in an environmentally sound manner in accordance with the environmental conditions specified in his environmental license and in accordance with applicable laws and regulations;

Officially inform the Ministry of Environment of any incident that has occured or that may have a negative impact on the environment during the transport of hazardous wastes within three days of occurance;

Immediately return the hazardous wastes to the waste generator if they are not accepted upon delivery by the facilities of storage, recovery, treatment or final disposal;

Submit all transport forms to the Ministry of Environment upon request, provided that the Ministry of Environment specifies in its request the deadline for submission of such documents;

Provide the Ministry of Environment with periodic reports, every three months, on the various transportation works carried out by him. The periodic reports are to include copies of all completed movement forms and documents related to incidents in case they occurred. Copies of these reports should be kept for a period of 5 years from the date of submission.

The Ministry of Environment has the right to impose new environmental conditions when necessary and request documents proving the implementation of these new conditions.

The hazardous wastes storage facility shall comply with the Environmental Management Plan and the environmental conditions specified in the environmental license and with the following:

Not to receive any hazardous wastes from a carrier who doesn’t have an environmental license as a carrier of hazardous wastes;

Not to accept to store any hazardous waste not accompanied by the hazardous waste movement form;

When requesting to transport any hazardous waste shipment, ensure that the hazardous waste movement form is completed and ensure that this form accompanies the shipment at all stages;

Not to accept to receive the hazardous wastes unless they are packaged in the manner stipulated in Article (14), Clause (1) of this Decree;

Ensure that the shipment of hazardous waste is not delivered or sent to any carrier or to any final recovery, treatment or disposal facility that are not licensed by the Ministry of Environment;

The conformity with the data documented on the hazardous wastes movement form prior to the commencement of storage;

Assume responsibility for any damage or change to the status of the hazardous wastes during the storage process and find appropriate ways to manage them in an environmentally sound manner in accordance with the environmental conditions specified in his environmental license and in accordance with the applicable laws and regulations;

Immediately return the hazardous wastes to their generator and at his expense if they are not accepted upon delivery due to their non-compliance;

Notify the Ministry of Environment, within 3 days of occurence, about any incident that has resulted in or may have a negative impact on the environment due to the poor storage of hazardous wastes;

Provide the Ministry of Environment with periodic reports, every three months, on the various storage activities carried out by the facility. The report should include the types and quantities of hazardous wastes, storage periods and incidents in the case they occured, the procedures and results of the monitoring process and copies of all completed hazardous waste movement forms. The reports are to be kept for a period of five years from the date of submission.

The Ministry of Environment has the right to impose new environmental conditions when necessary and request documents proving the implementation of these new conditions.

The hazardous wastes recovery facility, and/or treatment, and/or final disposal facility shall comply with the Environmental Management Plan and the environmental conditions specified in the environmental license and with the following:

Not to receive any hazardous wastes from a carrier who doesn’t have an environmental license as a carrier of hazardous wastes;

Not to accept any hazardous waste not accompanied by the hazardous waste movement form;

When receiving any hazardous waste shipment, ensure that the hazardous waste movement form is completed and ensure that this form accompanies the shipment at all stages;

Not to receive the hazardous wastes unless they are packaged in the manner stipulated in Article (14), Clause (1) of this Decree;

The conformity with the data documented on the hazardous wastes movement form before receiving it;

Immediately return the hazardous wastes to their sourec (the generator or storage facility) and at the expense of the owner if they are not accepted upon delivery due to their non-compliance;

Notify the Ministry of Environment, within three days of occurence, about any incident that has resulted in or may have a negative impact on the environment due to the poor recovery and/or treatment and/or final disposal of hazardous wastes;

Provide the Ministry of Environment with periodic reports, every three months, on the various activities regarding the recovery and/or treatment and/or final disposal carried out by the facility. The report should include the types and quantities of hazardous wastes, and incidents in the case they occured, the procedures and results of the monitoring process and copies of all completed hazardous waste movement forms. The reports are to be kept for a period of five years from the date of submission.

The Ministry of Environment has the right to impose new environmental conditions when necessary and request documents proving the implementation of these new conditions.
